# Alpha Skills — Quantitative Factor Research

Reference: [VernonOY/alpha-skills](https://github.com/VernonOY/alpha-skills/tree/main/skills)

Markets: A-share (China), Hong Kong, US equities — trading rules adapt per market.

## Skills

| Skill | Purpose | Example prompt |
|---|---|---|
| **alpha-discover** | Design factors from natural language | "find me a low-volatility factor" |
| **alpha-evaluate** | IC / ICIR / quintile / robustness | "evaluate reversal_5" |
| **alpha-mine** | Automated mining with IC screening | "mine 50 factors" |
| **alpha-library** | Factor registry and lifecycle | "show my factor library" |
| **alpha-backtest** | Single- or multi-factor portfolio backtest | "backtest pv_diverge + turnover" |
| **alpha-monitor** | IC decay and factor health | "check factor health" |
| **alpha-report** | Comprehensive analysis report | "generate factor report" |

## Defaults

- Reproducible pipelines: explicit data ranges and universe definitions.
- Report IC, ICIR, turnover, robustness — never just in-sample Sharpe alone.
- Register factors in alpha-library before backtest comparison.
- Flag look-ahead bias, survivorship bias, and overfitting when mining many factors.

## Correct vs wrong

```python
# CORRECT: explicit universe + date range, report ICIR
alpha_evaluate("reversal_5", universe="CSI500", start="2020-01-01", end="2024-12-31")

# WRONG: no universe, no date range, Sharpe only
alpha_evaluate("reversal_5")
```